Name the native plugin DLL after its file

libcarla_native-plugin.dll is linked with carla-native-plugin.def, whose
LIBRARY statement names it CarlaNativePlugin. GNU ld writes that name into
the DLL's export table, and a program linked to the DLL itself (Carla
installs no import library) imports CarlaNativePlugin.dll, a file that does
not exist, so it cannot start. lld names the DLL after its file anyway.
Name it after its file.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/source/plugin/symbols/carla-native-plugin.def b/source/plugin/symbols/carla-native-plugin.def
--- a/source/plugin/symbols/carla-native-plugin.def
+++ b/source/plugin/symbols/carla-native-plugin.def
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
-LIBRARY     CarlaNativePlugin
+LIBRARY     libcarla_native-plugin
 EXPORTS
     carla_get_native_rack_plugin @1
     carla_get_native_patchbay_plugin @2
